- Work reaches the trunk as one squash commit that `rk integrate <branch>` writes from a short-lived branch, once the `manual` stage passes. The branch name is `<type>/<slug>`, whose type matches the squash title's type, or the forge-minted `<issue-id>-<slug>`. Nothing else commits on `RK_TRUNK_BRANCH`, pushing the trunk is a separate operator action, and `--forge` sends one execution through a pull request instead.
